<title>POLAND: Elektromontaz-W to skip 1996 dividend.</title>
<headline>Elektromontaz-W to skip 1996 dividend.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-04-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shareholders of Polish Elektromontaz-Warszawa will vote on May 10 on the board's proposal to allot all the 1996 net profit of 1.8 million zlotys to reserve capital, the firm said in a Monday statement.</p>
<p>Shareholders will also vote on introducing to the bourse 4.5 million shares of the A series belonging to the state treasury and Mostostal Export.</p>
<p>The company now has 8,585,250 shares of a nominal value of one zloty each. The bourse trades 4,085,250 shares of the B and C series.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
